An r near the end of the preceding token pushes in the opposite direction;
selected corresponding letters in other scripts have similar responses.
Common function words and whitespace-separated words are much weaker.
Digits have a similar empirical contrast: preceding 7/8 push negative,
4/5/6 positive, and current 7 is most sensitive. Most other outputs are near zero.
This captures large rare bursts, not the many small lexical fluctuations.
