"""Negation detector (layer 0 MLP, down_proj component 1439).

The component writes a "negation" signal into the residual stream. It fires on:
  * " not" / "not" / " NOT": strength depends on the word before it. After do/does/did
    it is strong (~2.5); after other auxiliaries (is, was, could, has, will, ...) it is
    about 1; after "and"/"or"/a comma it is about 0; after if/but/when it turns negative.
  * the clitic "n't" ("'t" / "’t"): about half the " not" value for the same auxiliary.
  * " cannot", " dont": moderate, flat.
  * <|endoftext|> (a document boundary): strong, flat.
Rhetorical suggestions and questions flip it negative: "why not" (strongly), "How about",
and "Here's" (the 's of here's).
