the agent of a passive or a causal phrase: "produced by", "written by", "caused by",
"provided by", "posted by". Its size depends on the word just before "by":

- verbs of making, giving, causing, or publishing ("produced", "made", "provided",
  "caused", "written", "released") -> strongly positive;
- other past participles and verbs of action ("given", "used", "designed", "offered") ->
  moderately positive;
- sentence starts and punctuation before "by" ("By ...", ", by", "(by") and other nouns
  ("side by side") -> mildly positive;
- verbs of knowing, checking or defining ("seen", "known", "confirmed", "determined",
  "defined", "measured", "shown") -> near zero or negative.

