"""Negative response to gen spellings, strongest on the bare syllable.

Generation/generator and genetic words are strong; general is weaker.
A few birth/generation characters and g/je syllables in other scripts also
respond. Word-piece continuations and 'generation of' retain the response.
This approximates spelling sensitivity, not the meaning of arbitrary text.
