The response is primarily lexical: even log fragments inside longer words
can activate it. Standalone log is strongest, blogs and logging derivatives
are next, and errors, logic, and journals are weaker. Case and punctuation
matter. In particular, console.log is weaker than other .log uses. A few
non-English log/record spellings and logging API names are also recognized.
